  "evidence": "TEXT_E: Recruit 20,000 nurses and 10,000 doctors; faster, free NHS treatment; 10,000 more teachers; 6,000 more police and criminal justice reform; raise minimum wage; retain winter fuel payment; enhance support for children and pensioners; engage fully in Europe and support enlargement; action on global poverty and climate change; tackle drugs and causes of crime.\nTEXT_C: Leave the EU; UK Bill of Rights to prevent sovereignty transfer; national control of fisheries; increase defence spending and prioritise NATO; increase NHS funding with infection control focus and matron-style leadership; strong GMO labelling/protections and support for organics/higher animal welfare; monitor pollution health impacts; skills-based immigration with tighter monitoring and first-safe-country principle; 25,000 more police, visible community policing, and “life means life” for the worst crimes; protect jury trial/common-law safeguards; raise pensions and elderly care funding; 30,000 more teachers, smaller classes, discipline/selection and vouchers.",
  "reasoning": "Given the profile’s strongest weights on Care, Sanctity, Authority, and Loyalty, TEXT_C spans these foundations with NHS patient care paired with infection control (care/sanctity), robust law-and-order and institutional respect (authority), and sovereignty, defence, and controlled immigration (loyalty), while also providing social support. TEXT_E strongly emphasizes Care (NHS, welfare, minimum wage) and some Equality, but is comparatively light on Sanctity cues and frames loyalty around supranational engagement, so it maps less closely to the electorate’s heavier weighting on sanctity/authority/loyalty.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "winner": "TEXT_C"
